  "description": "カーソルに近い文字ほど滑らかに太くなり、隣の文字も中くらいの太さになって柔らかな山ができる。",
  "descriptionEn": "Letters thicken smoothly the closer the cursor gets; neighbours go medium, forming a soft hill of weight.",
  "focus": "距離に対してガウス曲線で減衰させるので、段差のない丸い山になる（下のカーブ）。文字の位置は動かず太さだけが変わるので、テキストプレッシャーより穏やか。",
  "focusEn": "Weight falls off along a Gaussian, so the hill has no steps (curve below). Positions never move — only weight — which makes it calmer than Text Pressure.",
  "caution": "半径が小さすぎると 1 文字だけ太る「ホバー」に、大きすぎると全体が太るだけになる。目安は字の高さの 1〜2 倍。文字を分割するときは aria-hidden ＋スクリーンリーダー用の文を別に置く。",
  "cautionEn": "Too small a radius becomes a single-letter hover; too large just bolds everything. Aim for 1–2× the letter height. When splitting, aria-hide the letters and keep a screen-reader copy.",
  "tips": [],
  "tipsEn": [],
  "recipe": "radius 50–100px / wght 400 → 900 / opsz 9 → 40 / falloff gaussian",
  "recipeEn": "radius 50–100px / wght 400 → 900 / opsz 9 → 40 / falloff gaussian",
  "curve": "standard",
