  "description": "上から吊るされた看板のように、語全体が上端を支点にゆっくり左右へ揺れ続ける。",
  "descriptionEn": "Like a sign hung from above, the whole word sways gently left and right around a pivot over its top edge.",
  "focus": "回転の中心（transform-origin）を語の外、上の釘に置くのがすべて。中心回転だと「首振り」だが、支点が上にあると下端ほど大きく動き、重さのある看板に見える。振れ幅は ±4° で十分。",
  "focusEn": "Everything hinges on putting transform-origin outside the word, at the nail above. Rotating around the centre looks like a head-shake; a pivot above makes the bottom swing furthest, reading as a heavy sign. ±4° is plenty.",
  "caution": "揺れ続けると読みにくいので、看板・店頭表示・遊びのある見出しなど一点に限る。両端で止まる ease-in-out にしないと機械的な振り子になる。reduced-motion では 0° で止める。",
  "cautionEn": "Constant sway costs legibility — limit it to one sign, shop label or playful heading. Use ease-in-out so it pauses at the extremes, or it looks mechanical. Hold at 0° under reduced motion.",
