  "titleEn": "Tategaki Reveal",
  "pattern": "text-tategaki-reveal",
  "duration": 3400,
  "motionDuration": 500,
  "easing": "easeOutExpo",
  "feelings": [
   "なめらか"
  ],
  "usages": [
   "テキスト"
  ],
  "description": "縦書きの文字が上から下へ1文字ずつ現れ、列は右から左へ進む。",
  "descriptionEn": "Vertical Japanese text appears one character at a time from top to bottom, and the columns advance from right to left.",
  "focus": "縦書きでは「次」が下にあるので、文字も上から落ちてくると流れと動きの向きがそろう。1 列が終わると左の列の頭に戻る。マス目は原稿用紙のイメージで、句読点はマスの右上に入り、列の頭に来る句読点はぶら下げ、小書きかなは前の列に残す（禁則）。かっこと長音は 90° 回る。",
  "focusEn": "In vertical writing the next character is below, so dropping each character from above aligns motion with reading direction. When a column ends, the reveal jumps to the top of the column on its left. Punctuation sits in the top-right of its cell; a comma or full stop that would start a column hangs below the previous one and small kana never start a column (kinsoku). Brackets and the long-vowel mark turn 90°.",
  "caution": "英数字は text-orientation（mixed / upright）と 2 桁の数字の縦中横（text-combine-upright: all）を決めておく。長い文で列が多いと右から左への移動が長くなるので、1 文字あたりの間隔を詰める。",
  "cautionEn": "Decide text-orientation (mixed / upright) for Latin letters and use tate-chu-yoko (text-combine-upright: all) for two-digit numbers. Many columns make the right-to-left journey long, so tighten the per-character delay.",
  "tips": [],
  "tipsEn": [],
  "recipe": "writing-mode: vertical-rl / y -20px → 0 / stagger 40–60ms / text-combine-upright: all (2 digits)",
  "recipeEn": "writing-mode: vertical-rl / y -20px → 0 / stagger 40–60ms / text-combine-upright: all (2 digits)",
