  "descriptionEn": "When the subtitle would collide with on-screen text at the bottom of the frame, it switches to vertical text at the right edge.",
  "focus": "画面下に看板やテロップ（焼き込みの文字）が出たら、字幕を右端の縦書きに移すのが日本語字幕の慣習。移動のアニメーションはせず、カットで位置ごと切り替える。縦は 1 行 11 字・2 行まで。",
  "focusEn": "When signs or burned-in captions appear at the bottom, Japanese subtitling moves the subtitle to vertical text at the right edge. It doesn’t animate across — it cuts to the new position. Vertical lines are capped at 11 characters, 2 lines.",
  "caution": "台詞は右、ナレーションは左など、位置に意味を持たせるなら作品の中で一貫させる。2 桁の数字は縦中横に。縦字幕は横より読むのに時間がかかるので、文字数を減らす。",
  "cautionEn": "If position carries meaning (dialogue right, narration left), keep it consistent throughout. Set two-digit numbers tate-chu-yoko. Vertical subtitles take longer to read, so trim the character count.",
  "tips": [],
  "tipsEn": [],
  "recipe": "≤ 11 chars / line (vertical) / ≤ 2 lines / right side by default / cut, no transition",
  "recipeEn": "≤ 11 chars / line (vertical) / ≤ 2 lines / right side by default / cut, no transition",
  "curve": "standard",
